  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marsabit Integrated Food Security and Resilience Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this project the Catholic Diocese of Marsabit aims to enhance food security and resilience for poor and vulnerable communities in Hula hula, Jaldesa and Bubisa locations in Marsabit county. It seeks to provide about 6000 men and women with: 
- improved income from higher crop and livestock production, achieved through training and the provision of relevant inputs;
- improved access to potable water through the construction and rehabilitation of water facilities,  training in safe hygiene and sanitation practices, and the establishment of water management committees;
- training and support for disaster preparedness and sustainable management of natural resources;
- reduced inter-community conflict, through measures to improve inter-faith and inter-community dialogue;
- identification of appropriate advocacy strategies, and training in advocacy and lobbying activities.

The project will seek to collaborate with the private sector and relevant government institutions at both at the county and national levels.</narrative>
  </description>
